<div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h1 class="h3 mb-2">Welcome to JobDesk</h1>
        <p class="mb-3">
            JobDesk is a work-order and operations app for a field-service business (installation crews, dispatch, materials).
            Robert Stewart built it with C# / ASP.NET Core and SQL, hosts it on AWS Lambda, and deploys with GitHub Actions.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mb-2">Try these</h2>
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-3">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" asp-controller="WorkOrders" asp-action="Index">Work orders</a>
            <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" asp-controller="Reports" asp-action="Index">Reports</a>
            <a class="btn btn-outline-dark" asp-controller="Ask" asp-action="Index">Ask</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="small text-muted mb-3">
            <li class="mb-1"><strong class="text-body">Work orders</strong> — search and filter jobs by status, customer, and crew.</li>
            <li class="mb-1"><strong class="text-body">Reports</strong> — totals by status, open jobs, and outstanding balance.</li>
            <li class="mb-1">
                <strong class="text-body">Ask</strong> — type a plain-English question about the data. Examples:
                <a asp-controller="Ask" asp-action="Index" asp-route-q="Work orders by status">Work orders by status</a>,
                <a asp-controller="Ask" asp-action="Index" asp-route-q="Outstanding invoice balance">Outstanding invoice balance</a>,
                <a asp-controller="Ask" asp-action="Index" asp-route-q="Overdue open work by crew">Overdue open work by crew</a>.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="small text-muted mb-3">
            All numbers and names are fictional sample data (about 3,000 work orders plus customers, crews, and invoices).
            Creating, editing, and uploads are turned off on this site so the data stays clean.
        </p>

        <p class="small mb-0 text-muted">
            <span class="text-body">How it works:</span>
            Browser → ASP.NET Core on AWS Lambda → SQL data;
            Ask → Amazon Bedrock over Databricks.
            <a href="https://github.com/rs691/jobDesk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
